' Singleton-diamond fixture — DIAMOND ARM 1 (depth 1; reaches the singleton
' at depth 2).
'
' A library-style service that needs the shared state, so it declares the
' singleton itself rather than being handed a reference. That is the correct
' use of the archetype, not a shortcut: threading a reference through every
' constructor is exactly what the DAT singleton exists to avoid.
'
' sgl_app_top ALSO declares sgl_shared_state directly, so the singleton is
' reached at depth 1 and depth 2 by different parents — the diamond. It is
' also declared TWICE by sgl_app_top (log and log2), which is what collides
' in ObjInstanceStore.
'
' Its own source has no #ifdef on the propagated symbol, so its
' preprocessedLines is identical regardless of what sgl_app_top exports —
' the same shape that hid the v1.54.4 defect.
OBJ
  shared : "sgl_shared_state"
  fmt : "sgl_fmt_util"

PUB start() : ok
  ok := shared.init()

PUB log_tick() : digits
  digits := fmt.width(shared.bump())

' Forwards the exportdef-gated value so the top level can reach it. Keeps
' trace_tag() referenced: its bytes are a test signal, and an unreferenced
' method is exactly what a future dead-code pass would drop — which would
' make the exportdef guard pass vacuously.
PUB trace() : tag
  tag := fmt.trace_tag()
